00:00:40.000 --> 00:01:42.000
Wisdom Powell is an associate professor of health behavior at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hills Gilling School of Global Public Health. Dr. Powell is also a faculty member at UNC's Limeberger Comprehensive Cancer Center and director of the UNC's Men's Health Research Lab. She is a nationally recognized psychological expert on the health disparities faced by minority boys and men. The term health disparities refers to differences in the availability and quality of care that are often experienced by members of minorities. groups. Powell's research focuses on the intersection of race, masculinity, health beliefs, and behavior, and she has been recognized by the American Psychological Association and the White House for her work. Welcome, Dr. Powell. Thank you for having me. How and why are lower-income black men and boys at a significant disadvantage in this country when it comes to health outcomes
威斯姆·鲍威尔（Wisdom Powell）是北卡罗来纳大学教堂山分校吉林斯全球公共卫生学院的健康行为副教授。鲍威尔博士还是北卡罗来纳大学林伯格综合癌症中心的教员，兼北卡罗来纳大学男性健康研究实验室的主任。她是全国公认的心理学专家，专注于少数族裔男孩和男性面临的健康差距问题。“健康差距”一词是指少数族裔成员经常经历的医疗服务可用性和质量上的差异。鲍威尔的研究重点是种族、男子气概、健康信念和行为的交叉点，她的工作得到了美国心理学协会和白宫的表彰。欢迎你，鲍威尔博士。谢谢邀请我来。为什么以及如何让低收入的黑人男性和男孩在这个国家的健康结果处于明显的劣势？

