We know that when people have lower income, they have lower access to resources, they have lower access to opportunities for upward social mobility, they have lower access to health care and mental health care. And because of those sort of essential factors, you see this relationship that manifests as one that suggests that being lower income means that you will automatically have poor health status. I think that in order to get beneath that correlation, you have to look at it. at some of the mechanisms driving it, including poor access to care and also poor access to jobs and other forms of socioeconomic opportunity. Mascular norms, as they're called in psychological research, are sometimes described as the rules of masculinity.
我们知道，当人们收入较低时，他们获得资源的渠道较少，获得向上社会流动机会的渠道较少，获得医疗保健和心理健康服务的渠道也较少。正因为这些基本因素，你会看到这种关系表现为：收入较低意味着你将自动拥有不良的健康状况。我认为，为了探究这种相关性背后的原因，你必须审视导致它的某些机制，包括获得护理的机会较差，以及获得工作和其他形式的社会经济机会的机会较差。在心理学研究中被称为“男子气概规范”的概念，有时被描述为男子气概的规则。

